<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nashua,_New_Hampshire> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Nashua** is a city in southern [New Hampshire](:New_Hampshire), United States. As of the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_census), it had a population of 91,322, the second-largest in northern [New England](:New_England) after nearby [Manchester](:Manchester%2C_New_Hampshire). Along with Manchester, it is a [seat](:County_seat) of New Hampshire's most populous county, [Hillsborough](:Hillsborough_County%2C_New_Hampshire).Built around the now-departed [textile](:Textile) industry, in recent decades Nashua's economy has shifted to the [financial services](:Financial_services), [high tech](:High_tech), and [defense](:Arms_industry) industries as part of the [economic recovery](:Massachusetts_Miracle) that started in the 1980s in the [Greater Boston](:Greater_Boston) region. Major private employers in the city include [Nashua Corporation](:Nashua_Corporation), [BAE Systems](:BAE_Systems), and [Teradyne](:Teradyne). The city also hosts two major regional medical centers, [Southern New Hampshire Medical Center](:Southern_New_Hampshire_Health_System) and [St. Joseph Hospital](:St%2E_Joseph_Hospital_%28Nashua%2C_New_Hampshire%29). The South Nashua commercial district is a major regional shopping destination, lying directly on the Massachusetts border and taking advantage of New Hampshire's lack of sales tax. It is anchored by the [Pheasant Lane Mall](:Pheasant_Lane_Mall) and numerous smaller shopping centers.Nashua was three times named one of the \"Best Places to Live in America\" in annual surveys by [*Money*](:Money_%28magazine%29) magazine, most recently in 2022. It is one of many cities nicknamed \"[Gate City](:Gate_City)\" because they are seen as the entry point, or gateway, to a region."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
