<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Juba_International_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Juba Airport** ([IATA](:IATA_airport_code): **JUB**, [ICAO](:ICAO_airport_code): **HJJJ**) is an airport serving [Juba](:Juba), the capital city of [South Sudan](:South_Sudan). The airport is located 5 km (3 mi) northeast of the city's central business district, on the western banks of the [White Nile](:White_Nile). The city and airport are located in South Sudan's [Central Equatoria State](:Central_Equatoria).It is one of the two international airports in [South Sudan](:South_Sudan), the other being [Malakal Airport](:Malakal_Airport). Juba Airport handles international and local airlines, cargo air traffic and chartered commercial flights. It is also used by the South Sudanese military and by the United Nations [UNMISS](:UNMISS), UN Humanitarian Air Services [UNHAS](:UNHAS), World Food Program [WFP](:WFP), ICRC and many NGOs for relief flights for the country."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
