<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mountain_View,_Arkansas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Mountain View** is the largest city in and the [county seat](:County_seat) of [Stone County, Arkansas](:Stone_County%2C_Arkansas), United States. Located in [the Ozarks](:The_Ozarks), the city has a rich tradition of preserving folk music and culture. The city's economy is largely based on tourism related to its title as the \"Folk Music Capital of the World\". Mountain View hosts the Arkansas Folk Festival in April, various folk artists at [Ozark Folk Center State Park](:Ozark_Folk_Center_State_Park) throughout the year, and weekly music gatherings on the courthouse stage that are free and open to the public during summer months. The city is also known for outdoors recreation opportunities, including [Blanchard Springs Caverns](:Blanchard_Springs_Caverns), [trout](:Trout) fishing on the [White River](:White_River_%28Arkansas%29) and the [Ozark National Forest](:Ozark_National_Forest)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
