<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cut_Nyak_Dhien_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cut Nyak Dhien Airport (Indonesian: Bandar Udara Cut Nyak Dhien) (IATA: MEQ, ICAO: WITC) is an airport located in Nagan Raya Regency, Aceh, Indonesia. The airport is located 26 kilometers from Suka Makmue, 46 kilometers from Meulaboh, West Aceh Regency, and 347 kilometers from the city of Banda Aceh. The airport serves both Suka Makmue the capital Nagan Raya Regency and Meulaboh the capital of West Aceh Regency."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Zintan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Zintan (Arabic: الزنتان Latin: Tentheos, Berber language: Zintan or Tigharmin or Tiɣaṛmin, meaning \"small castles\") is one of the biggest cities in north western Libya, situated roughly 136 kilometres (85 mi) southwest of Tripoli, in the area. The city and its surrounding area has a population of approximately 50,000."@en .
