<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Durham_(Mulock)_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Durham (Mulock) Airport**, formerly [TC](:Transport_Canada) [LID](:Location_identifier): **CNH3**, was located 6 [nautical miles](:Nautical_mile) (11 km; 6.9 mi) northwest of [Durham](:Durham%2C_Ontario) in the community of [Mulock](:Mulock%2C_Grey_County), [Ontario](:Ontario), Canada."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chapais,_Quebec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Chapais** is a community in the [Canadian province](:Provinces_and_territories_of_Canada) of [Quebec](:Quebec), located on [Route 113](:Quebec_Route_113) near [Chibougamau](:Chibougamau) in the [Jamésie](:Jam%C3%A9sie_Territory%2C_Quebec) region. It is surrounded by, but not a part of, the [local municipality](:Types_of_municipalities_in_Quebec) of [Eeyou Istchee James Bay Regional Government](:Eeyou_Istchee_James_Bay_Regional_Government). The community was first settled in 1929, when prospector Léo Springer discovered deposits of copper, silver and gold in the area, and was incorporated as a city in 1955. It was named for [Thomas Chapais](:Thomas_Chapais)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
