<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ostend–Bruges_International_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Ostend–Bruges International Airport** (Template:Lang-nl ([IATA](:IATA_airport_code): **OST**, [ICAO](:ICAO_airport_code): **EBOS**), commonly known simply as **Ostend Airport** (Template:Lang-nl, is an [international airport](:International_airport) located 2.7 [nautical miles](:Nautical_mile) (5.0 km; 3.1 mi) south southwest of [Ostend](:Ostend), [West Flanders](:West_Flanders) in the [Flemish Region](:Flemish_Region) of [Belgium](:Belgium), near the coast and about 25 km (16 mi) from the city centre of [Bruges](:Bruges). Although freight transport is the focus of a large proportion of its activities, the airport is increasingly used for passenger flights, mainly [charter](:Charter) and holiday flights organised by tour operators. It is also often used for private business flights."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
