<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bauru-Arealva_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Moussa Nakhl Tobias State Airport (IATA: JTC, ICAO: SBAE), commonly known as Bauru–Arealva Airport is the main airport serving Bauru and Arealva, Brazil. It is named after the Lebanese businessman and vice-mayor Moussa Nakhl Tobias (1940-2003), who immigrated to Brazil in 1959 and established himself in Bauru. It is operated by Rede Voa."@en .
