<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Boundary_Bay_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Boundary Bay Airport** or **Vancouver/Boundary Bay Airport** ([IATA](:IATA_airport_code): **YDT**, [ICAO](:ICAO_airport_code): **CZBB**) is located beside [Boundary Bay](:Boundary_Bay) and 2.5 [nautical miles](:Nautical_mile) (4.6 km; 2.9 mi) east of [Ladner](:Ladner%2C_British_Columbia) in [Delta](:Delta%2C_British_Columbia), [British Columbia](:British_Columbia), Canada, 8.5 NM (15.7 km; 9.8 mi) south southeast of [Vancouver](:Vancouver) and close to the [Point Roberts-Boundary Bay border crossing](:Point_Roberts%E2%80%93Boundary_Bay_Border_Crossing). The airport, which opened on July 11, 1983, serves mostly [general aviation](:General_aviation) and includes facilities for aircraft maintenance, flight training and parking. In 2020 and 2021, Boundary Bay airport was ranked as the [busiest airport in Canada by aircraft movements](:List_of_the_busiest_airports_in_Canada).The airport is classified as an [airport of entry](:Airport_of_entry) by [Nav Canada](:Nav_Canada) and is staffed by the [Canada Border Services Agency](:Canada_Border_Services_Agency) (CBSA). CBSA officers are available on call to handle entry for aircraft carrying no more than 15 passengers."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
