<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Varfolomeyevka_(air_base)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Varfolomeyevka (also given as Varfolomeyevka South) is an air base in Primorsky Krai, Russia. During the 1980s it was one of 17 tactical reconnaissance aircraft bases in the Soviet Union, and one of two such bases in the Far East region along with its sister base Vozzhayevka. In the first decade of the 21st century the airfield hosted regiments of the Russian 11th Air and Air Defence Forces Army."@en .
