<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Airports_Authority_of_India> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Airports Authority of India,** or **AAI,** is a Statutory Body under the [ownership](:Ownership) of the [Ministry of Civil Aviation](:Ministry_of_Civil_Aviation_%28India%29), [Government of India](:Government_of_India). It is responsible for creating, upgrading, maintaining, and managing civil aviation infrastructure in India. It provides Communication Navigation Surveillance/Air Traffic Management (CNS/ATM) services over Indian [airspace](:Airspace) and adjoining oceanic areas. AAI is currently managing a total of 137 airports, including 34 international airports, 10 [Customs Airports](:Customs_Airport), 81 domestic airports, and 23 [Civil enclaves](:Civil_enclave) at defense airfields. AAI also has ground installations at all airports and 25 other locations to ensure the safety of aircraft operations. AAI covers all major air routes over Indian landmass via 29 [Radar](:Radar) installations at 11 locations along with 700 [VOR](:VHF_omnidirectional_range)/DVOR installations co-located with [Distance Measuring Equipment](:Distance_Measuring_Equipment) (DME). 52 runways are provided with [Instrument landing system](:Instrument_landing_system) (ILS) installations with Night Landing Facilities at most of these airports and an Automatic Message Switching System at 15 Airports."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
