<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Korea_Airports_Corporation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Korea Airports Corporation was established in 1980 in Seoul, South Korea to carry out construction, checks and balances, management and operation of airports and to manage air transportation efficiently. As an organization specializing in airport management, KAC manages and operates total of 14 airports in Korea including Gimpo, Gimhae, Jeju, Daegu, Muan, Cheongju, and Yangyang international airport. KAC also manages the Area Control Center, 10 VOR/TACs and Korea Civil Aviation Training Center. Its headquarters are on the property of Gimpo International Airport in Gangseo-gu, Seoul."@en .
