<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chibougamau> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Chibougamau** (Template:IPA-fr is the largest town in [Nord-du-Québec](:Nord-du-Qu%C3%A9bec), central [Quebec](:Quebec), Canada. Located on Lake Gilman it has a population of 7,504 people ([2016 Canadian Census](:2016_Canadian_Census%29). Chibougamau is surrounded by, but not part of, the [local municipality](:Types_of_municipalities_in_Quebec) of [Eeyou Istchee James Bay Regional Government](:Eeyou_Istchee_James_Bay_Regional_Government).Due to its remoteness from [Lac Saint-Jean](:Lac_Saint-Jean) (over 200 km (124 mi) south-east) and [Abitibi-Témiscamingue](:Abitibi-T%C3%A9miscamingue) (over 250 km (155 mi) south-west) areas, Chibougamau provides services for a few smaller communities surrounding it ([Mistissini](:Mistissini%2C_Quebec), [Oujé-Bougoumou](:Ouj%C3%A9-Bougoumou) and [Chapais](:Chapais%2C_Quebec%29) and for the regional [resource-based](:Natural_resource) industries. Despite Chibougamau's remoteness, it is only about as far north as [Winnipeg](:Winnipeg), and is south of any part of the mainland of [England](:England).Nearby are [Lake Aux Dorés](:Dor%C3%A9s_Lake), which is fed by the [Chibougamau River](:Chibougamau_River) from the larger [Chibougamau Lake](:Chibougamau_Lake), after which the town was named. *Chibougamau* means \"Gathering place\" in the [Cree language](:Cree_language). The neighbouring [Cree](:Cree) village of Oujé-Bougoumou has the same name with a more traditional Cree spelling.The area surrounding Lake Gilman is Obalski Park. Its amenities include a beach, pier, picnic tables, cabins, among others. The many trails allow for hiking, cycling, cross-country skiing, or even snowmobiling through the park's [boreal forest](:Taiga).Access to the town is by [Route 167](:Quebec_Route_167) from Lac Saint-Jean and by [Route 113](:Quebec_Route_113) from [Lebel-sur-Quévillon](:Lebel-sur-Qu%C3%A9villon). [Chibougamau's airport](:Chibougamau/Chapais_Airport) is along Route 113, about halfway to Chapais."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
