<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Isortoq_Heliport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Isortoq Heliport (IATA: IOQ, ICAO: BGIS) is a heliport in Isortoq, a village in the Sermersooq municipality in southeastern Greenland. The heliport is considered a helistop, and is served by Air Greenland as part of a government contract."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Churchill_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Churchill Airport** ([IATA](:IATA_airport_code): **YYQ**, [ICAO](:ICAO_airport_code): **CYYQ**) is located 3 [nautical miles](:Nautical_mile) (5.6 km; 3.5 mi) east southeast of [Churchill](:Churchill%2C_Manitoba), [Manitoba](:Manitoba), Canada. The airport serves the town of Churchill and the surrounding region. Although it is a small domestic airport, it handles a relatively high number of passengers throughout the year as Churchill is a major destination for [ecotourism](:Ecotourism) and scientific research. Churchill Airport also serves as a transfer airport for passengers and cargo travelling between [Winnipeg](:Winnipeg) and remote communities in the [Kivalliq Region](:Kivalliq_Region) of [Nunavut](:Nunavut)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
