<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Flemish_Region> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Flemish Region (Dutch: Vlaams Gewest, pronounced [ˌvlaːms xəˈʋɛst]; French: Région flamande; German: Flämische Region), usually simply referred to as Flanders (Dutch: Vlaanderen [ˈvlaːndərə(n)]; French: Flandre [flɑ̃dʁ]; German: Flandern [ˈflandɐn]), is one of the three regions of Belgium—alongside the Walloon Region and the Brussels-Capital Region. It occupies the northern part of Belgium and covers an area of 13,522 km2 (5,221 sq mi) (44.4% of Belgium). It is one of the most densely populated regions of Europe with around 490/km2 (1,300/sq mi)."@en .
