<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Anaconda,_Montana> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Anaconda**, county seat of [Deer Lodge County](:Deer_Lodge_County%2C_Montana), which has a [consolidated city-county](:Consolidated_city-county) government, is located in southwestern [Montana](:Montana), United States. Located at the foot of the [Anaconda Range](:Anaconda_Range) (known locally as the \"Pintlers\"), the [Continental Divide](:Continental_Divide_of_the_Americas) passes within 8 mi (13 km) south of the community. As of the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_Census) the population of the consolidated city-county was 9,421, and the US Census Bureaus's 2015-2019 [American Community Survey](:American_Community_Survey) showed a median household income of $41,820. Anaconda had earlier peaks of population in 1930 and 1980, based on the mining industry. As a consolidated city-county area, it ranks as the ninth most populous city in Montana, but as only a city is far smaller. Central Anaconda is 5,335 ft (1,626 m) [above sea level](:AMSL), and is surrounded by the communities of Opportunity and West Valley.The county area is 736.53 square miles (1,907.6 km2), characterized by densely timbered forestlands, lakes, mountains and recreation grounds. The county has common borders with Beaverhead, Butte-Silver Bow, Granite, Jefferson and Powell counties."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
