<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ruby,_Alaska> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Ruby** ([Koyukon](:Koyukon_language): *Tl'aa'ologhe*) is an incorporated town in central western Alaska, situated on the south bank of the [Yukon River](:Yukon_River) at the northwesternmost tip of the [Nowitna National Wildlife Refuge](:Nowitna_National_Wildlife_Refuge). It is accessible only by boat or air. A formerly sizeable gold-mining and lumbering town servicing the region, at the [2010 census](:2010_United_States_Census) the population was just 166, with only a general store and post office remaining as businesses, down from 188 in 2000."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
