<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kuala_Lumpur_International_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Kuala Lumpur International Airport** (**KLIA**) ([IATA](:IATA_airport_code): **KUL**, [ICAO](:ICAO_airport_code): **WMKK**) is [Malaysia's main international airport](:Busiest_airports_in_Malaysia). It is located in the [Sepang District](:Sepang_District) of [Selangor](:Selangor), approximately 45 kilometres (28 mi) south of [Kuala Lumpur](:Kuala_Lumpur) and serves the [city's greater conurbation](:Greater_Kuala_Lumpur).KLIA is the largest and busiest airport in [Malaysia](:Malaysia). In 2020, it handled 13,156,363 passengers, 505,184 tonnes of cargo and 124,529 aircraft movements. It is the world's [23rd-busiest airport by total passenger traffic](:World%27s_busiest_airports_by_passenger_traffic).The airport is operated by [Malaysia Airports](:Malaysia_Airports) (MAHB) Sepang Sdn Bhd and is the major hub of [Malaysia Airlines](:Malaysia_Airlines), [MASkargo](:MASkargo), [Batik Air Malaysia](:Batik_Air_Malaysia), [UPS Airlines](:UPS_Airlines), [MYAirline](:MYAirline) and [World Cargo Airlines](:World_Cargo_Airlines), and the major operating base of [AirAsia](:AirAsia) and [AirAsia X](:AirAsia_X)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
