<http://dbpedia.org/resource/José_María_Velasco_Ibarra_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "José María Velasco Ibarra Airport (Spanish: Aeropuerto J.M. Velasco Ibarra) (IATA: MRR, ICAO: SEMA) is an airport serving Macará, a city in the Loja Province of Ecuador. Macará is on Ecuador's border with Peru. The airport is named for José María Velasco Ibarra, a former president of Ecuador. The airport is within the city, and has mountainous terrain north, and rising terrain in all other quadrants. The Macara non-directional beacon (Ident: MAC) is located on the field."@en .
