<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Infraero> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Empresa Brasileira de Infraestrutura Aeroportuária** (abr. **Infraero**) is a Brazilian [government corporation](:Government_corporation) founded in 1973, authorized by Law 5,862, being responsible for operating the main [Brazilian commercial airports](:List_of_the_busiest_airports_in_Brazil). In 2011 Infraero's airports carried 179,482,228 passengers, 1,464,484 tons of cargo, and operated 2,893,631 [take-offs](:Takeoff) and [landings](:Landing). Presently it manages 45 airports.The company is present all over Brazil and employs approximately 23,000 employees and subcontracted workers nationwide. It is headquartered in the Infraero Building, in [Brasília](:Bras%C3%ADlia), [Federal District](:Federal_District_%28Brazil%29)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
