<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mangnai> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Mangnai** also known as **Mang'ai** or **Mangya** ([Chinese](:Simplified_Chinese_characters): 茫崖; [pinyin](:Pinyin): *Mángyá*) is a [county-level city](:County-level_city) in the northwest of [Qinghai Province](:Qinghai_Province), China, bordering [Xinjiang](:Xinjiang) to the north and west. It is under the administration of [Haixi Mongol and Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture](:Haixi_Mongol_and_Tibetan_Autonomous_Prefecture). It is one of the most remote cities in China, the closest other city, [Ruoqiang](:Ruoqiang_County), is located 350 kilometres (220 mi) away. In 2018 it had a population of 63,000. The name Mangnai is based on the Mongolian word for 'forehead'.It was formed in 2018 when the Mangnai and [Lenghu](:Lenghu) administrative zones merged to establish the county-level city of Mangnai."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
