<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kristiansand_Naval_Air_Station> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kristiansand Naval Air Station (Norwegian: Marinens flystasjon Kristiansand) was a water military air base operated by the Royal Norwegian Navy Air Service between 1919 and 1940. Situated at Tangen in the city center of Kristiansand, Norway, it consisted of three hangars. The station was to house both reconnaissance and fighter aircraft."@en .
