<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Taranto-Grottaglie_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Taranto-Grottaglie \"Marcello Arlotta\" Airport (Italian: Aeroporto di Taranto-Grottaglie \"Marcello Arlotta\") (IATA: TAR, ICAO: LIBG) is an airport serving Taranto and Grottaglie, both comunes in the province of Taranto in Italy. The airport is located 1.5 km (0.8 NM) from the city of Monteiasi, 4 km (2.2 NM) from Grottaglie and 16 km (8.6 NM) from Taranto. It is named for Marcello Arlotta (1886-1918), an Italian aviator."@en .
