<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sliač_Airport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Sliač Airport** ([IATA](:IATA_airport_code): **SLD**, [ICAO](:ICAO_airport_code): **LZSL**) or, historically, *Letisko Tri Duby* (literally, \"The Three Oaks Airport\") is a military airport in central [Slovakia](:Slovakia) situated between the towns of [Zvolen](:Zvolen) and [Banská Bystrica](:Bansk%C3%A1_Bystrica) and near the spa town of [Sliač](:Slia%C4%8D). The airport has one runway which is 2,400 m long (18/36). The airport is used only by the military since October 2021, when the airport has been closed to all civilian traffic. In 2022, the airport operator company Letisko Sliač a.s. went into liquidation and all airport equipment was sold."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
